  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For an **upper-upscale** hotel project in North America, owners and developers commonly shortlist brands such as **Omni Hotels & Resorts**, **Hard Rock Hotels**, **Margaritaville Hotels & Resorts**, **Le Méridien**, **Westin**, **Marriott Hotels & Resorts**, **Kimpton**, **Hyatt Centric**, and **Hilton Garden Inn** depending on the asset’s positioning.[3][4][7]\n\nIf the question is specifically about brands that perform well in *guest-satisfaction or market-ranking* surveys in the upper-upscale tier, **Omni** and **Hard Rock** are the most consistently leading names in J.D. Power’s upper-upscale category, with **Margaritaville**, **Le Méridien**, **Marriott/Westin**, and **Kimpton** also appearing near the top.[3][4][7]\n\nFor a broader development shortlist, owners often look at the parent companies’ portfolios and flagships that are active in North America, especially **Marriott**, **Hilton**, **Hyatt**, and **IHG**, because these groups control many of the brands most often considered for upper-upscale projects.[1][11][13]\n\nA practical shortlist by *brand family* would usually include:\n- **Omni Hotels & Resorts**[3][4]\n- **Hard Rock Hotels**[3][4]\n- **Margaritaville Hotels & Resorts**[3][4][7]\n- **Le Méridien**[3][4]\n- **Westin**[3][4]\n- **Marriott Hotels & Resorts**[4][20]\n- **Kimpton**[7]\n- **Hyatt Centric**[7]\n- **Hilton Garden Inn**[7]\n\nIf you want, I can also turn this into a **developer-style shortlist by use case**: urban, resort, lifestyle, or conversion.",
